cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >-
  Cite the release or commit of kernelgecp used in your work, together with
  relevant upstream methods and numerical libraries.
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
title: "kernelgecp: Fermionic kernel cross approximation and verified numerical research"
authors:
  - name: "kernelgecp contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tripp-smith/gecp-kernel-structure"
url: "https://github.com/tripp-smith/gecp-kernel-structure"
abstract: >-
  Lean formalization and reproducible numerical tools for Gaussian elimination
  with complete pivoting and the fermionic kernel. The Python interface supports
  cached physical Green-function bases, complex matrix batches, imaginary-time
  and Matsubara evaluation, finite-query numerical certificates, and an optional
  Rust backend for 128-bit reference time evaluation. Formal exact-run theorems,
  sampled physical comparisons, and conditional numerical certificates retain
  distinct scopes.
keywords:
  - "Gaussian elimination with complete pivoting"
  - "fermionic Green functions"
  - "cross approximation"
  - "verified numerics"
  - "Lean"
  - "Rust"
